    <tags>notes notepad encrypted sqlite markdown dictation portable</tags>
    <summary>Open-source notes app for Windows with rich text, tags, instant search, dictation, sketches and optional encryption.</summary>
    <description>Notes that keep up. A searchable, organized replacement for the 80-tab Notepad workflow: rich notes with inline images and tables, instant full-text search, and optional password protection for the whole database.

- Rich text, lists, tables, rules, inline images, spell check, word wrap, line numbers, title colors, font controls and a color picker with a desktop eyedropper
- Instant search across titles, text and tags, with filters, quoted phrases and saved searches; Ctrl+F searches the open note without changing it
- Nested, colorable groups, tag filters, flexible sorting and adjustable sidebar density; Ctrl+Z undoes sidebar moves, reorders and deletes
- Syntax highlighting detected paragraph by paragraph, so one note mixes prose with PowerShell, JSON, SQL, C#, Python and ten more without picking a language
- Hyperlinks: Ctrl+K links the selection, typed URLs auto-link, links survive pasting from browsers and Word, and only web and mail addresses ever open
- Wikilinks between notes, with incoming and outgoing links, links to notes that do not exist yet, a graph and a heading outline
- Offline dictation (Ctrl+M): record and transcribe locally, then insert text, an editable recording or both. The speech engine and model download on first use for your processor
- Edit recordings on the waveform with undo; store lossless FLAC and export WAV or MP3
- SketchPad (F7): pen, shapes, fill, text labels and eraser on single keys; print the drawing inline and double-click it later to keep editing
- Killculator (F9): a themed calculator under the notes list that prints the result or the whole running equation into the note
- Custom fonts for header, sidebar and note text independently, from any installed font or a dropped .ttf/.otf
- Autosave, saved cursor and scroll positions, and Markdown or sanitized HTML preview beside the note or on its own
- Storage: one SQLite database in a configurable location, portable next to the exe if you like, with create, rename, switch and relocate in the Manage databases dialog
- Version history (Alt+H), a 30-day trash, note templates (Alt+T), daily notes (Alt+D), headings with an outline, checkbox lines and pinned notes
- Scheduled backups with retention, immediate backup (Alt+B), failure warnings and a restore check that reads the copy without touching your notes
- Lock now (Ctrl+Shift+U) closes a password-protected notepad without quitting, and it locks itself when Windows locks or sleeps, or after an idle time you choose
- Quick note: a small capture box from the tray icon, the taskbar jump list or Win+Alt+N
- Import a folder of notes from a KillerNotes export, an Obsidian vault or another Markdown export, with a preview first; KillerNotes also appears under Open with for .md and .txt
- Password protection: optional SQLCipher AES-256 encryption of the whole database, set, changed or removed at any time, with no recovery for a lost password
- Share notes or databases with optional passwords; export notes as Markdown, text, rich text or HTML, with pictures, sketches and recordings
- Command line for search, editing, sharing, export, templates, groups, tags, recovery and backups
- Keyboard-first: every function has a shortcut, F1 opens the visual keyboard map, and the whole app scales for accessibility from 70% to 250%
- Thirteen themes including a full 98SE recreation; Dark, Light, Black and 98SE each carry eight accent colors for 41 looks in all
- Localized in twenty languages, falling back to English
- One self-contained Windows EXE, no runtime install; installs per-user or for all users, or runs portable
- GPLv3, local-only, no account, no telemetry
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SteveTheKiller/KillerNotes/releases/tag/vREPLACE_VERSION</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
